\title{Elliptical Slice Sampling Backend for ratio Models}
\description{
Elliptical Slice Sampling (ESS) backend for models with Gaussian priors.
ESS is particularly efficient for:
\itemize{
\item Random effects (which have N(0, sigma^2) priors)
\item Spatial effects (which have GMRF priors)
\item GP effects (which have multivariate normal priors)
}
}
\details{
ESS has several advantages over HMC for models with Gaussian priors:
\itemize{
\item \strong{No tuning parameters}: Unlike HMC step size, ESS adapts automatically
\item \strong{Efficient for high-dimensional Gaussians}: Exploits prior structure
\item \strong{Exact transitions}: No discretization error (unlike leapfrog)
}

ESS works by:
\enumerate{
\item Drawing a proposal from the prior (Gaussian)
\item Defining an ellipse through current state and proposal
\item Slice sampling along this ellipse
}

Non-Gaussian parameters (variance components, correlations) are updated
using adaptive random-walk Metropolis-Hastings within each ESS iteration.
}
